  "_comment": "Upstream source for every mark in apps/docs/public/logos/. Vector sources run through normalize-logos.mjs (nested <svg>); raster sources are downscaled to 180px and inlined as a data URI in the same 120x90 canvas. Always pick the variant that reads on white — npm's README background.",
  "_verify": "After regenerating, open each mark at height=90 on white and LOOK at it. Two silent failure modes bit us: a truncated PNG still reports valid dimensions to `file` but renders as a partial band, and a mark that colours itself with a root-level fill goes black if the attribute is dropped.",

